//? Title: QFT: actual gate states, comb phases and simulated storage
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Hadamards, controlled phase rotations and final bit swaps produce a unitary
Fourier transform. The native producer now captures the actual state after each
simulator gate and validates the complete finite register before it touches
caller storage. The original 16-state comb supported at 1,5,9,13 is retained.
Its frequency probabilities and phases are directly inspectable; a state-vector
simulation is a classical exponential-storage calculation, not a quantum
speedup.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

$$ y_k=\frac1{\sqrt N}\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}x_j e^{2\pi i j k/N},\qquad N=2^n. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/qft_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::qft_trace(a::qft_comb(2, 4, 1), 2);
    std::print("\n| actual gate ordinal | native kind (0 H,1 phase,2 swap) | control | target | radians | " "actual post-gate amplitude0 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.gates.size(); ++i) {
        auto &e = t.gates[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | ({},{}) |\n", i, int(e.kind),
                   e.control, e.target, e.angle, e.after[0].real(),
                   e.after[0].imag());
    }

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual input amplitude at 1\n{} + {} i",
                       t.initial[1].real(), t.initial[1].imag()));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual first-gate amplitude at 1\n{} + {} i",
                       t.gates[0].after[1].real(), t.gates[0].after[1].imag()));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual final amplitude at 1\n{} + {} i",
                       t.run.state[1].real(), t.run.state[1].imag()));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/qft_tiny.svg");
}
```
